SUMMARY:Deadline: EFA SHIFT x Momus Residency 2027: six-month programme for
  New York artists who write and writers who make art (USD 2\,000 honorariu
 m)
DESCRIPTION:A new iteration of EFA's SHIFT Residency\, run with the art cri
 ticism platform Momus and focused on where artistic practice meets critica
 l writing. Four New York-based practitioners whose work moves between visu
 al art and art criticism (artists who write\, or writers who make art) spe
 nd six months at EFA Studios\, mentored by artist and writer Ajay Kurian (
 founder of NewCrits).\n\nOrganisation: Elizabeth Foundation for the Arts (
 EFA Studios) with Momus\nLocation: EFA Studios\, 323 West 39th Street\, Ne
 w York City\, USA. In person\; applicants must be based in New York.\nAwar
 d: Artist honorarium of USD 2\,000\, within a six-month residency at EFA S
 tudios with monthly critical seminars and mentoring. No application fee st
 ated.\nDuration: Six months\, July to December 2027\n\nMore: https://eliza
 bethfoundation.submittable.com/submit/366863/open-call-for-efa-shift-x-mom
 us-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://elizabethfoundation.submittable.com/submit/366863/open-call-for
 -efa-shift-x-momus-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
LOCATION:EFA Studios\, 323 West 39th Street\, New York City\, USA. In perso
 n\; applicants must be based in New York.
END:VEVENT
