SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: Schomburg Center Scholars-in-Residence 2027-28 
 (NYPL\, Harlem\; USD 35\,000 long-term or USD 3\,000 a month short-term\; 
 playwrights and creative writers eligible)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nResidential fellowships for
  work on the history\, politics\, literature and culture of peoples of Afr
 ican descent that needs the Schomburg Center's collections. WHO: the libra
 ry's programme page opens both fellowships to postdoctoral scholars\, inde
 pendent researchers and creative writers (novelists\, playwrights\, poets)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture\, The Ne
 w York Public Library\nLocation: Schomburg Center\, Harlem\, New York City
 \, USA. RESTRICTED: US citizens\, permanent residents and foreign national
 s with the legal right to work in the United States.\nAward: Long-term fel
 lowship: USD 35\,000 stipend. Short-term fellowship: USD 3\,000 per month 
 for one to three months. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: Long-ter
 m: one semester (September to December 2027\, or January to May 2028)\; th
 e application portal describes it as six months. Short-term: one to three 
 continuous months.\n\nMore: https://www.nypl.org/about/fellowships-institu
 tes/schomburg-center-scholars-in-residency/application?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
